# Public-export rules — ORDERED, first match wins. `+ ` includes, `- ` excludes. Globs: `*` (no slash), `**` (any).
# Applied to `git ls-files` only, so untracked files (.env, keys, build output) can never cross by construction.
# Decisions: cline_docs/reviews/open-source-readiness-2026-09-03/{PLAN,SCRIPT-TRIAGE,SEED-INVENTORY,CLAUDE-DIR-SCAN}.md
# Anything not matched by a `+` is EXCLUDED (final rule). Edit the decision docs first, then this file.

# ── Rule 1 (Steve): server management NEVER exports ─────────────────────────────
- cline_docs/**
- "cline_docs/**
- infra/**
- ops/**
- temp-scripts/**
- userInstructions/**
- scripts/archive/**
- scripts/deploy/**
- scripts/mcp-tools-output/**
- .github/workflows/production-deploy.yml
- .github/workflows/production-rollback.yml
- .github/workflows/docker-services-deploy.yml
- .github/workflows/deployment-status.yml
- .github/workflows/uptime.yml
- .github/workflows/test-deployment.yml
- .github/workflows/build-parity-dark-run.yml
- .env.production.template
- prisma/generated/**
- **/*.backup.*
- .claude/knowledge/branding/**
- ecosystem.config.js.bak
- docker-compose.yml
- docker-compose.dev.yml
- nginx-oauth-fix.conf
- execute-node-upgrade.sh

# ── scripts/: OPS + ARCHIVE classes (SCRIPT-TRIAGE.md). Tests that run NOWHERE are dropped by the
